ference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "577c8913fb2227c19e517b6ce8a43fd1d47b0bd3bb57fcfeec02a3e2e905f3f5" "basis" 786 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2) \\\\  & ≈1.107.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =1.107$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "577c8913fb2227c19e517b6ce8a43fd1d47b0bd3bb57fcfeec02a3e2e905f3f5" "basis" 786 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b79df5d8e5d16fb4a9e8dca5d5f06b09d67e2cdebc7a13e7049f602b56100f29" "basis" 786 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radi