orm $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-3)| \\\\  & ≈1.893.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =1.893$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6817cff3d59030ae52c31cbe6cce1976efecf258b0407977fee39bebe2c5fca0" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.389\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.983\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/c5d36b72e7e2ff6754152a559d64bf3610708c9a2d3790c859bc9abacc9220b6.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6817cff3d59030ae52c31cbe6cce1976efecf258b0407977fee39bebe2c5fca0" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "593dc74e8a4e76014ae3d42c44d406328cfd5e52a50335d8a3a09606641c1cd3" "basis" 1908 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-17524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=-2+6\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-3)| \\\\  & ≈1.893.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =1.893$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f69c634627088c92d4dd39d4befab06742d0d5ff839e69bfd1e3cab496d4371"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.389\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.983\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=1+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2) \\\\  & ≈1.107.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =1.107$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f69c634627088c92d4dd39d4befab06742d0d5ff839e69bfd1e3cab496d4371"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.456\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.817\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-8076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=5-\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-8076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-1}{5})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{5})| \\\\  & ≈2\\pi -0.197\\,39… \\\\  & ≈6.086.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{26}$ and $\\theta =6.086$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"question" "q-8076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f69c634627088c92d4dd39d4befab06742d0d5ff839e69bfd1e3cab496d4371"} {"question" "q-8076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/state.json" "file_sha256" "91858153e065fc52f322f05a766da8ec1503a9d5794e88a4be0c7aa228505886"} {"ques