demy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/example-5282.json" "file_sha256" "7f524b18b769ac0d55df9cbc1290dbde07217aa610c315aafd5f29df1b63e18c"} {"question" "e-5280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/c93c5bf19eefeb4da980b81d46c4df10b3ff10aca21937aed885ef4111b1c9a7.png), shown in the following Argand diagram, in exponential form.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/335311049419928acc946721242c6e8e4096313dca1290b89b1cc7a2c30748fd.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/example-5280.json" "file_sha256" "e6024bac1b5a96a01b245cdaf60d9e411ab86e126dadc5988f4cd9b8e0fe9e8c"} {"question" "e-5280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/5d6456ae3c5f168a14e761b44085defd76cd2292e8fa8d9b0eedf2cb55d97563.png)\n\nTo write it in the form ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/0eb9bfc5066fce3fe0434f4dedf05cea2fff1e2fe38b32d4223eaf177ca2b654.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/d3e8106a9b65dceed9a9c4e6fbc6341c0268517854b72f6e34fc3ec80117b915.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/6017ce5c562b2c1a2d1a47371c54820b04852fb851056aa171f88c411d92bd45.png) we first calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/e3862c77b505ea48e95acf4d632fa692c866c65079a2ac6b17543fd54e1c20ca.png)\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/d0bd5d7fc7f1d7b487fd940af95b5abb7e2fb134c02a55dbf9eb7d191abccca8.png)\n\nNow, since ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/c93c5bf19eefeb4da980b81d46c4df10b3ff10aca21937aed885ef4111b1c9a7.png) lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/f49e0503f6588c93dd1fd274c63f60c06b0eb77d5dce2d12dba750107139f124.png) as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/96e40550e19a81ffb655cd359242d8b0a37b1dde12e442252f976397a09a9760.png)\n\nto three decimal places.\n\nFinally, substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/5dcf5f8d9a0eb6d36f76152105bcb5a9af61a34bc99719183df2044d7f113edb.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/11dd78699cf02b8b10f1bd6dc78ee987d26954fc8b51a2e8327c2f24b5552458.png) into ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/9ea3d5e030449e3b1da133b0aa004c6d26702021bf66e5672abe2bdd2c69eb9b.png) we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/dd0d831b250bbf985783cbb745a23c709a481ba08018395c683c3e2d4b00284a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/example-5280.json" "file_sha256" "e6024bac1b5a96a01b245cdaf60d9e411ab86e126dadc5988f4cd9b8e0fe9e8c"}] "usage" {"q-71983" [] "q-8076" [] "q-17517" [] "q-71978" [] "q-8075" [] "q-107428" [] "e-5280" [] "q-17524" [] "e-5282" []} "basis" 2796 "retractions" [[17592186088232 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nWrite the complex number $z =-1 + \\textrm{i}$ in exponential form."] [17592186087998 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/898/Source/Images/q-17517.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $re^{\\textrm{i}θ}$, giving $θ$ in radians to three decimal places."] [17592186277519 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/assets/ba77669a8e0ffd3e69bfc8e5322d7042c318a55b4cd486ac1fac591d3b016e43.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to the nearest tenth."] [17592186088231 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/c5d36b72e7e2ff6754152a559d64bf3610708c9a2d3790c859bc9abacc9220b6.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form."] [17592186087476 :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form\n\n$$\nz = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nr= \\mid z \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arg(z)\n$$\n\nwe first calculate $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr = \\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nθ = \\arg (z) &= \\arctan (\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\\n&= \\arctan (1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{π}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nr=4\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\ninto\n\n$$\nz=re^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\nz = 4\\sqrt{2}\\,\\textrm{e}^{\\pi\\textrm{i}/4}\n$$"] [17592186087475 :question/problem "Write the complex number $z$, shown in the following Argand diagram, in exponential form.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/898/Source/Images/a0fe46e109e3784d66675d033d5fdbd8.png)"] [17592186087475 :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= x + \\textrm{i}y \\\\\n&=-3 + 2\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form\n\n$$\nz = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nr= \\mid z \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arg(z)\n$$\n\nwe first calculate $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr = \\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-3)^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\arg (z) &= π - \\mid \\arctan (\\frac{y}{x}) \\mid \\\\\n&= π - \\mid \\arctan (\\frac{2}{3}) \\mid \\\\\n&= π - 0.588 \\\\\n&= 2.554\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places.\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{13}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=2.554\n$$\n\ninto\n\n$$\nz=re^{\\textrm{i} \\theta}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\nz = \\sqrt{13}\\,\\textrm{e}^{2.554\\,\\textrm{i}}\\,\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186085000 17592186085001 17592186085002 17592186085003 17592186085004 17592186086318 17592186086319 17592186086320 17592186086321 17592186086322 17592186086324 17592186086325 17592186086326 17592186086327 17592186086328 17592186266098 17592186266099 17592186266100 17592186266101 17592186266102 17592186277521 17592186277522 17592186277523 17592186277524 17592186277525 17592186277535 17592186277536 17592186277537 17592186277538 17592186277539 17592186338274 17592186338275 17592186338276 17592186338277 17592186338278] "immutable_fields" [[17592186084999 :answer-field/correct] [17592186084999 :answer-field/id] [17592186084999 :answer-field/key] [17592186084999 :answer-field/typ